==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|fair|way}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈfɛɹweɪ/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈfɛəweɪ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛə(ɹ)weɪ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|golf}} The area between the [[tee]] and the [[green]], where the [[grass]] is cut short.
# Any [[tract]] of [[land]] free from [[obstacle]]s.
# {{lb|en|military}} A channel either from [[offshore]], in a [[river]], or in a [[harbor]] that has enough [[depth]] to accommodate the [[draft]] of large [[vessel]]s. (JP 4-01.6)
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[navigable]] [[channel]] in a [[harbour]], [[offshore]] etc; the usual [[course]] taken by [[vessel]]s in such places.
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Treasure Island|text=By good fortune, paddle as I pleased, the tide was still sweeping me down; and there lay the ''Hispaniola'' right in the '''fairway''', hardly to be missed.}}
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|part=I|passage=Lights of ships moved in the '''fairway'''—a great stir of lights going up and going down.}}

